WEBVTT

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.350
Ladies and gentlemen, I give you the Chris Dempsey Root.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.910
*music*

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.560
*outro music*

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:04.420
- Bye.

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:00.570
Thank you.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:11:00.000
I haven't played in the Eerie in about six years, so thank you for coming out to see us and being here for the Jazz Festival.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:06.020
pretty cool thing and blues festival excuse me i'm probably not going to do a ton of talking today

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:11.590
because uh i'm not very good at it so there it is uh that last tune was a tune called speak low

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:20.280
we're going to play a tune now called the cape verdean blues and uh we've never played this

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:21.380
before so it's probably gonna be okay

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:02.310
Bye.

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:35.280
*music*

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:01.540
I don't know.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:32.200
Thank you.

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:09.220
We'll be right back.

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:31.890
.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:13.670
*music*

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:20.030
. . .

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:33.600
Bye.

00:23:00.510 --> 00:23:01.250
Thank you.

00:24:42.860 --> 00:24:43.360
Thank you.

00:24:44.140 --> 00:24:48.110
This next one's going to feature Dr. Alan Zurcher.

00:24:49.580 --> 00:24:51.720
He says it's overrated, but it means something.

00:24:52.690 --> 00:24:58.060
And I was a doctor on my tombstone.

00:24:58.140 --> 00:24:58.400
Got it.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.150
This is a tune entitled Central Park West.

00:28:05.920 --> 00:28:06.600
Bye.

00:28:30.030 --> 00:28:30.640
Yeah.

00:32:27.390 --> 00:32:28.160
Alan Zurchin.

00:32:39.630 --> 00:32:39.930
going to feature

00:32:39.930 --> 00:32:43.490
Alec Doobie on

00:32:43.490 --> 00:32:47.410
the vibes on a

00:32:47.410 --> 00:32:47.830
tune called

00:32:47.830 --> 00:32:49.560
Azul Serapid,

00:32:50.040 --> 00:32:52.370
which is Irish

00:32:52.370 --> 00:32:52.910
for I don't know

00:32:52.910 --> 00:32:53.390
what that means.

00:32:55.120 --> 00:32:59.000
If you know what

00:32:59.000 --> 00:32:59.510
that means, I

00:32:59.510 --> 00:33:00.000
have a dollar in

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:07.620
for you. It's a monopoly dollar, but it's a dollar.

00:44:36.780 --> 00:44:40.070
This next tune is the polar opposite of that.

00:44:41.300 --> 00:44:43.640
It's called Killer Joe.

00:45:16.890 --> 00:45:17.350
said something.

00:55:04.160 --> 00:55:04.720
Killer joke.

00:55:11.210 --> 00:55:14.370
There's this crazy lady behind the stage that's just screaming every time.

00:55:15.150 --> 00:55:18.860
I know her, so it's great, but she's not my mom.

00:55:18.980 --> 00:55:22.300
If anyone wants to know, my mom's out there somewhere probably also screaming.

00:55:34.350 --> 00:55:36.390
I'm going to play a tune, this is Coltrane, right?

00:55:36.700 --> 00:55:37.020
Coltrane?

00:55:37.140 --> 00:55:37.260
Yeah.

00:55:38.790 --> 00:55:40.630
By John Coltrane, entitled Cousin Mary.

00:57:00.760 --> 00:57:01.220
BELL RINGS

00:58:01.340 --> 00:58:01.830
.

01:06:17.720 --> 01:06:20.160
We're going to marginally slow it down a little bit.

01:06:20.160 --> 01:06:21.320
This is a tune called "Lora."

01:06:56.460 --> 01:06:59.480
*music*

01:07:00.030 --> 01:07:15.430
Oh, my God.

01:07:32.910 --> 01:07:36.820
*music*

01:11:00.380 --> 01:11:20.800
Oh

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:24.630
- This is Laura.

01:12:24.630 --> 01:12:27.380
- I think we're lucky we have one or two more tunes here

01:12:27.380 --> 01:12:29.860
before Tony Gray takes over and the gang.

01:12:30.480 --> 01:12:36.600
This next tune is a Joe Henderson tune that I haven't played in 20 years, so I did look at it.

01:12:37.420 --> 01:12:38.560
I have a little credit here.

01:12:39.760 --> 01:12:41.920
There's a tune called Serenity. It's by Joe Henderson.

01:12:54.060 --> 01:12:58.190
We have an unruly vibes player up here who's making all these unruly requests like,

01:12:58.190 --> 01:12:58.970
Can I play?

01:13:01.310 --> 01:13:02.530
So he's going to lead it off.

01:21:25.340 --> 01:21:27.970
So apparently Alan's mic was off for the entire solo.

01:21:28.070 --> 01:21:30.000
So we're going to go ahead and play that song all over again.

01:21:30.920 --> 01:21:33.920
Because we wouldn't want you to miss all the interesting things that came out of it.

01:21:35.660 --> 01:21:39.430
Looks like we only have time for one more tune.

01:21:39.830 --> 01:21:41.700
And I lost the vote.

01:21:42.760 --> 01:21:44.420
So we're going to play a tune.

01:21:44.480 --> 01:21:44.900
It's a good tune.

01:21:44.960 --> 01:21:45.340
Don't get me wrong.

01:21:45.440 --> 01:21:47.840
I mean, I picked it, so it must be good.

01:21:48.760 --> 01:21:51.220
This is a tune called Cherokee.

01:21:53.140 --> 01:21:56.050
Consequently, my wife, I was going to play Giant Steps at the end of this,

01:21:56.090 --> 01:22:00.000
and she goes, that's so, like, such a jazzy thing.

01:22:00.000 --> 01:22:01.260
to do. You shouldn't do that.

01:22:02.550 --> 01:22:04.230
She's out there somewhere probably blushing

01:22:04.230 --> 01:22:06.250
and angry at me, and I have the couch

01:22:06.250 --> 01:22:07.730
all made up for this evening, so it's fine.

01:22:08.390 --> 01:22:10.190
But we're going to play Cherokee instead,

01:22:11.230 --> 01:22:12.410
which should make her happy.

01:28:30.540 --> 01:28:32.690
.

01:30:43.240 --> 01:30:43.920
Thank you.

01:30:44.470 --> 01:30:45.830
Alan Surcher on saxophone.

01:30:45.930 --> 01:30:47.550
Alec Duby on the vibes.

01:30:48.200 --> 01:30:49.640
Paul LaDuke on bass.

01:30:49.760 --> 01:30:51.240
John Bacon Jr. on drums.

01:30:51.420 --> 01:30:52.140
I'm Chris Dempsey.

01:30:52.220 --> 01:30:52.820
Thank you very much.
